From the massive amounts of feedback, I've decided the following:

1. I will be flexible with my build. This includes swapping some
artifacts, but when MR is so easy to get (either from a cloak or an
artifact), I think SDSM's here to stay.
2. Daggers have replaced Mjollnir, at least for the early-game.
3. EotA seems quite good, particularly for the branch-porting. I've
read a lot about its use in stash-management, particularly with Soko.
I think I'll give it a try.
4. Rings have now changed to free action and alternating between
levitation, increase damage, slow digestion (early-game) and the
teleport and polymorph sets. (Again, this is subject to what I
actually get.)
5. I'm not digging for victory.
6. I will be taking my time and clearing out every level. Always.
7. I can't really see me casting spells, can someone reassure me of
this being possible with a Valk?
8. I don't really need a Self-Notes.txt file for files; I've tried it
before and it makes the game more laboured without much of a payoff.
9. "In some of your later posts, you seemed overly concerned about
generating too many artifacts.  This isn't all bad; it's a stupid idea
to make Sting, for example, but for Odin's sake, get Mojo and your
quest artifact as soon as you can." Ray, I agree there, it's probably
a better idea for survival.
10. What gauntlets are better than power, dexterity? I suppose I could
use them, if I decide to make spellcasting an option...
11. How do you even get Magicbane as a Valk, short of wishing for it?
12. I will be taking my time.
13. Credit cloning is amazing.
14. Intrinsics are the way to win.
15. Holy water will breed like rabbits where I'm concerned.
16. #twoweapon is happening. Screw shields. (Unless I find a shield of
reflection before any other source of it).
17. Clairvoyance after divine protection.
18. Elbereth. Often.

I think that's it for now.

